gaZV(){return"Guide"},
gaZS(){return"Audio Editor guide"},
gaZN(){return"The Audio Editor is a multitrack studio: stack clips on lanes, shape them, add effects, then play or export. Tap any clip to edit it."},
gaZU(){return"Top toolbar"},
gaZT(){return"Undo and redo every edit. With clips selected, copy, cut, paste at the playhead, or delete them across lanes. Play or stop, toggle Loop, toggle Snap to grid, export the mix, or clear everything. Generate\u2026 builds a fresh tone, noise or silence clip on its own lane, and the zoom buttons stretch or squeeze the timeline (Fit shows the whole arrangement at once). If you mark a range while Loop is on, playback loops just that selection instead of the whole arrangement."},
gaZI(){return"Building a track"},
gaZH(){return"Use Add clip to drop in a sound: a sample from the Sound Library, an imported audio file, a song or score (Add music), a sample lifted from a module or pack, or a ready-made beat or groove. Add track makes a new lane; drag a clip along a lane to move it in time."},
gaZK(){return"Editing a clip"},
gaZJ(){return"Tap a clip to open its inspector: set volume, fade in and out, trim the start and end, then Split at the playhead, Duplicate, Reverse, change speed (Slower or Faster), Crossfade into the next clip, Freeze to a plain audio take, or Remove it. Use the small check on a clip to select several for batch actions."},
gaZM(){return"Effects and mixing"},
gaZL(){return"Effects live in chains at four scopes: a single clip, a whole track, a bus, or the master output. Add effects like Reverb, Delay, Compressor, Gate, Chorus, Pan or Gain, and automate any control with breakpoints over time. Each track has its own volume and pan."},
gaZP(){return"Linked editors"},
gaZO(){return"A music clip (shown with a note badge) stays linked to the notation editors. Open in editor takes it to the Score or Tab Workshop; when you Send to Audio Editor there, it updates this same clip in place. You can also send it one way to the Advanced Tracker."},
gaZR(){return"Keyboard shortcuts"},
gaZQ(){return"On a keyboard: Space plays or stops; Delete removes the selected clips."},
gow(){return"Help for this screen"},
gb4X(){return"Getting around"},
gb4W(){return"\u2022 Learn: each game card teaches one skill.\n\u2022 Create: Score Workshop, Tab Workshop, Tracker, Loop Studio and the Audio Editor open from the authoring menu (piano icon).\n\u2022 Tools: Transcribe, Tuner, Sound Lab, Library and the Song Book sit alongside them.\n\u2022 The ? on any screen explains that screen; this one explains the app."},
gb5c(){return"Guitar Tab"},
gb5b(){return"\u2022 Tap a fret cell and type a fret number, or use the on-screen keypad.\n\u2022 The duration strip sets the note length; letters add notes at the caret.\n\u2022 Patterns and Chords insert ready-made material.\n\u2022 Tuning and Capo change what each string sounds.\n\u2022 Mic captures a performance onto the grid.\n\u2022 Notation shows the staff above the tab; Export saves MusicXML, MIDI or PDF."},
gb52(){return"Practice with your song"},
gb51(){return"\u2022 Pick a song; the app separates it into stems (vocals, drums, bass, other).\n\u2022 Choose a separator: faster, or higher quality.\n\u2022 Mute or solo stems, loop a section, and slow it down.\n\u2022 Songs longer than 10 minutes are refused on phones to bound memory."},
gb5e(){return"Tracker"},
gb5d(){return"\u2022 Rows are time; the columns are channels.\n\u2022 In the note column type A\u2013G then an octave digit.\n\u2022 Instrument column: the instrument-pool number. Effect column: command + 2 hex digits.\n\u2022 Long-press a cell or a column header for the block and channel menus.\n\u2022 Space plays from the cursor; the toolbar sets tempo and edit step."},
gb4T(){return"Chart editor"},
gb4S(){return"\u2022 One bar sits between each |; two chords split a bar.\n\u2022 % or an empty bar holds the previous chord.\n\u2022 [A] starts a section; [A] x2 repeats it.\n\u2022 The key menu sets the key; transpose moves the whole chart.\n\u2022 Practice loop plays the chart with the backing band."},
gb5a(){return"Sound Lab"},
gb59(){return"\u2022 Pick a voice or sample, then shape it with the controls.\n\u2022 Preview plays the current sound.\n\u2022 Save to My Instruments to reuse it in scores and loops."},
gb5i(){return"Voice Lab"},
gb5h(){return"\u2022 Choose a neural voice; the first use downloads a small model.\n\u2022 Enter text and preview it through the selected voice.\n\u2022 Speed and pitch change the delivery.\n\u2022 Save a voice for lessons and narration."},
gb58(){return"Song Book"},
gb57(){return"\u2022 Songs you save are listed here.\n\u2022 Open loads a song into an editor.\n\u2022 The \u22ee menu renames, duplicates or deletes.\n\u2022 Import adds a file; licences are shown before use."},
gb50(){return"Library"},
gb5_(){return"\u2022 Browse bundled songs, exercises and soundfonts.\n\u2022 Filter by source or tag.\n\u2022 Tap an item to preview and open it.\n\u2022 Licence notes explain what you may share."},
gb56(){return"Setlist"},
gb55(){return"\u2022 Add songs in playing order.\n\u2022 Drag to reorder.\n\u2022 Start begins the set; the next song advances at the end.\n\u2022 The set length estimates the timing."},
gb4V(){return"Gig mode"},
gb4U(){return"\u2022 Large, legible controls for the stage.\n\u2022 Swipe or tap to move between songs.\n\u2022 Auto-advance follows the setlist.\n\u2022 The screen stays awake while active."},
gb5g(){return"Tuner"},
gb5f(){return"\u2022 Play a note; the needle shows how far off it is.\n\u2022 Set the reference pitch (A4) for the ensemble.\n\u2022 Pick an instrument preset for the string names.\n\u2022 Green means in tune."},
gb54(){return"Sample Extractor"},
gb53(){return"\u2022 Load a song or a sample.\n\u2022 Drag the handles to set start and end.\n\u2022 Loop previews the selection.\n\u2022 Save writes a new sample or soundfont entry."},
gb4Z(){return"Import"},
gb4Y(){return"\u2022 Pick a file: MusicXML, MIDI, ABC, MuseScore, GP, LilyPond and more.\n\u2022 Photos of scores use OMR, which downloads a model on first use.\n\u2022 Licensed material is marked; export rules are shown.\n\u2022 The result opens in the Score or Tab Workshop."},
