gbjC(){return"On the beat, or off?"},
gbjB(){return"Usually the notes land right ON the beats \u2014 count 1-2-3-4 and each note lands on a number. Steady and square."},
gbjA(){return'Syncopation pushes notes OFF the beat, onto the "and" in between. The accent lands where your ear didnt expect it \u2014 thats the kick you feel in pop and jazz.'},
gbjY(){return"Two or three in a beat"},
gbjW(){return'Normally a beat splits into TWO even halves: "1-and". Two eighth notes.'},
gbjX(){return'A triplet squeezes THREE equal notes into that same beat: "trip-o-let". It gets a little 3 above it.'},
gbiT(){return"Decorating a note"},
gbiU(){return"Ornaments are little signs that dress up a note. A trill (tr) shakes quickly between the note and the one just above it."},
gbiV(){return"A turn (a sideways S) curls AROUND the note: the note above, the note, the note below, then back. A mordent is just one quick flick up and back."},
ga4t(){return"Label the Form"},
gasX(){return"Hear the sections; name the shape (ABA\u2026)"},
gb3B(){return"What is the form? (same colour = same tune)"},
gb3A(){return"Listen"},
gbhW(){return"The shape of a piece"},
gbhV(){return"Music is built from sections. Here is a little tune \u2014 call it section A. Whenever it comes back, it is A again."},
gbhU(){return"A different tune is a new letter \u2014 section B. Tune, different tune, then the first tune again makes the form A-B-A. Lots of songs are shaped this way!"},
ga4V(){return"Which Mode?"},
gato(){return"Major, minor or Dorian?"},
gbd9(){return"Listen! Which mode is it?"},
ga1n(){return"Major"},
ga1o(){return"Minor"},
gbd8(){return"Dorian"},
gbiP(){return"Three colours of scale"},
gbiN(){return"A major scale sounds bright and happy. Listen to it climb."},
gbiO(){return"A minor scale sounds darker \u2014 its 3rd, 6th and 7th steps sit a little lower."},
gbiM(){return"Dorian is like minor, but its 6th step is raised \u2014 so it sounds minor with a brighter twist. That one note is the whole secret!"},
gaoZ(){return"Textbook"},
gbpI(){return"Read"},
gbpF(){return"Work through music from the very start. Each topic has a short lesson (see it, hear it) and games to practise it."},
gbpz(){return"Lesson coming soon"},
gbpH(){return"Read the lesson"},
gbpG(){return"Practise"},
gaki(){return"See the form"},
gakh(){return"Play the whole piece"},
gb3r(){return"Tap a block to hear that section."},
gakD(){return"See the harmony"},
gb4v(){return"Tap a chord to hear it."},
gOS(){return"Home (tonic)"},
gOR(){return"Away (subdominant)"},
gOQ(){return"Tension (dominant)"},
gb3S(){return"Home"},
gb3R(){return"Away"},
gb3Q(){return"Tension"},
gaR8(){return"Harmony"},
gaRi(){return"Analyse the harmony"},
gCc(){return"Inspect (tap a note)"},
gaR7(){return"Form"},
gaR3(){return"Circle of fifths"},
gaRg(){return"Tension"},
gagw(){return"Voice leading"},
gaRh(){return"No parallel 5ths or 8ves \u2713"},
gaRe(){return"Parallel fifths"},
gaRf(){return"Parallel octaves"},
gagv(){return"Non-chord tones"},
gahb(){return"perfect cadence"},
gahd(){return"half cadence"},
gahe(){return"plagal cadence"},
gahc(){return"deceptive cadence"},
